> # A new session has one state, the root.
> state log
@  0  (root)


> # Each command that changes the simulation adds a state.
> time advance 1m
advanced time by 1m to 1970-01-01T00:01:00Z

> time advance 2m
advanced time by 2m to 1970-01-01T00:03:00Z

> state log
@  2  time advance 2m
│
○  1  time advance 1m
│
○  0  (root)


> # A command that only reads adds nothing, and neither does one that fails.
> time show
1970-01-01T00:03:00Z

> time advance 1000000years
error: duration out of range for the simulated clock

> state log
@  2  time advance 2m
│
○  1  time advance 1m
│
○  0  (root)


> # `state switch` makes an earlier state current again. The next change then
> # grows a branch beside the old one.
> state switch 1
switched to state 1

> time show
1970-01-01T00:01:00Z

> time advance 5m
advanced time by 5m to 1970-01-01T00:06:00Z

> state log
@  3  time advance 5m
│
│ ○  2  time advance 2m
├─╯
○  1  time advance 1m
│
○  0  (root)


> # Every state stays reachable.
> state switch 2
switched to state 2

> time show
1970-01-01T00:03:00Z

> state log
○  3  time advance 5m
│
│ @  2  time advance 2m
├─╯
○  1  time advance 1m
│
○  0  (root)


